abstract: >-
  A C++23 earthquake detection and early-warning pipeline with hand-written
  inference and no machine-learning runtime: miniSEED ingestion, a learned
  6 s window detector (with a STA/LTA reference trigger and a streaming
  transformer), P/S picking, network association, location and magnitude,
  replayed against AFAD and KOERI data. Includes the model weights, the tools
  that reproduce every number in the accompanying paper, and the benchmarks.
keywords:
  - seismology
  - earthquake early warning
  - earthquake detection
  - deep learning
  - real-time
